list of topics:

1. goal of the thesis

The goal of this thesis is to implement an RDC layer into contiki-ng and evaluate the performance of several RDC protocols for the SX1280 radio which is a 2.4 GHz LoRa radio. 


2. different steps in the project
The project can be divided into different parts. 

The radio is used for this project is the sx1280 which is not supported by default in contiki-ng. This means a custom driver is required to be able to use it. This part of the project was done by 2 previous master students.

The next step is to implement an RDC layer into contiki-ng. 

The RDC layer is part of the MAC layer and lies between the MAC protocol and the physical layer. The RDC layer is responsible for turning the physical radio on and off at the right time in order to save energy. A more advanced RDC protocol will also synchronize sending times to previously known wake up times in order to avoid collisions.

In order to implement the RDC layer correctly i make use of the previous version of contiki-ng called contiki-os. This version has a built in RDC layer. While both version of contiki are not completly the same, contiki-os can still be used to create a good structure for the RDC layer. 

After having implemented the RDC layer structure i started working on the first RDC protocol. In order to start of simple, i started with nullRDC. This protocol doesn't do anything extra. nullRDC adds the header to the packet and then transmits it. 

when creating contiki-ng they didn't just completly remove the RDC layer, instead they hardcoded nullRDC into CSMA. This means that in order to be able to use an RDC protocol in contiki-ng, CSMA needs to be modified. The hardcoded nullRDC in CSMA has to be removed and instead the packet needs to be send to the RDC layer. 




